Instead of giving only an ascension report, it may be more interesting 
to describe my diverse attempts, eventually successful, to ascend a 
Flame mage. I needed five tries, which does not seem too bad, 
considering that in my early slashem times I had to run seven valkyries 
to ascend the first one (and that in nethack, my first ascension was a 
valkyrie for whom I needed a single attempt -- after a number of 
unsuccessful archeologist trials).

Nevertheless, given how far my first attempt at a flame mage went, I 
should have succeeded that one. But he died a very stupid death. In 
fact, three of the five were ascendable, and three of the four deaths 
were stupid (if not all four of them :-) ).

Here are excerpts from the score records on the two computers, on which 
I played. The sequence these were played in was Erestorm, Firefly, 
Fireball, Firepin, and Firenail. So after the desaster with Erestorm, 
each character got a little farther than his predecessor, but no doubt 
Firepin should have made it, as you will see when I give a short 
breakdown of his life cycle below.


